 "capsule": "In the last phase of Cnut the Great's North Sea Empire, his son Harthacnut ruled Denmark and England jointly from 1040 until he collapsed and died at a wedding feast in June 1042. Norway's King Magnus the Good then claimed the Danish throne under an earlier mutual-succession pact with Harthacnut and asserted a rival claim to England against the newly acclaimed Edward the Confessor, a dispute over the English crown that persisted until Magnus's own death in October 1047 ended the Norwegian bid.",
